abstract: >-
  CGMPy is a modular Python library for Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)
  data analysis. It loads CGM exports from common devices (Dexcom, Libreview,
  Medtronic, Tandem), validates and processes the time-series, computes the
  full battery of clinical glucose metrics (mean, GMI, TIR/TAR/TBR, SD, CV,
  MAGE, MODD, CONGA, LBGI/HBGI, GRI, GRADE, ADRR, M-Value, J-Index) and
  renders standard visualisations (AGP, daily traces, statistical
  distributions, dashboards). It ships a pregnancy-specific facade with
  trimester breakdowns and the 63-140 mg/dL gestational cutoffs.
